From b42bc6d8470b139eedbdb1e9ba2eaab419050ccf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DCS <claude@dcs.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:43:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] server: hide sensitive content until the PIN is entered

An asset tagged IMMICH_SENSITIVE_TAG (default Sensitive) or a tag under it,
or showing a person marked sensitive, keeps its place in the timeline,
search and albums, but its thumbnails and image originals are served as a
blurred placeholder (its thumbhash, enlarged and marked) and its video and
video original are refused, until the session is unlocked with the PIN.
A Live Photo's motion part follows its still. Shared links always get the
placeholder. Real media of sensitive assets is sent uncached.

GET /api/assets/:id/sensitive says whether an asset is hidden.
GET/PUT /api/people/:id/sensitive marks a person sensitive; showing them
again needs an unlocked session. People are kept in the video index schema
(sensitive_person), so this part needs immich-video-face's schema.
